# React coding rules

Detail: [docs/knowledge/react/README.md](../docs/knowledge/react/README.md), [fe-next-app-router.mdc](./fe-next-app-router.mdc)

## Data fetching

- ❌ `useEffect` + `fetch` to load data in components
- ✅ Server Components fetch on server (async page/layout)
- ✅ TanStack Query in client hooks (`features/*/hooks/`) for client-side cache/refetch
- ✅ Server Actions for mutations; hooks invalidate queries after success

## Client boundary

- Default **Server Components**; `'use client'` only when needed (hooks, browser APIs, event handlers)
- Priority: **RSC** → **Server Action** → **Client Component** (`"use client"` = last choice)

## State

- ❌ Deep prop drilling across many layers
- ✅ URL/searchParams for shareable UI state (filters, pagination) when appropriate
- ✅ React Context for localized tree state (theme, form wizard)
- ✅ Zustand for cross-feature client state (`features/*/stores/` or `shared/`)

## Callbacks & memoization

- ❌ Inline anonymous functions passed to `memo()` children or heavy lists without need
- ✅ `useCallback` when passing stable callbacks to memoized children or virtualized lists
- ❌ Derived state synced via `useEffect` when it can be computed during render

## Components

- Business logic stays in features (`hooks/`, `services/`, `actions/`) — not in presentational UI
- See [fe-services-layer.mdc](./fe-services-layer.mdc) for API access
